AWS EC2 URL: http://3.148.195.189/

2. Configuration Steps

- Amazon S3 Deployment

Bucket Creation: Log in to S3 and create a bucket (e.g., swe645-saikarthick-portfolio). Uncheck "Block all public access".

Permissions: Apply a Bucket Policy to allow public read access (s3:GetObject).

Upload Files: Upload index.html, survey.html, error.html, and photo.webp.

Static Hosting: Enable "Static website hosting" in the bucket properties. Set index.html as the index document and error.html as the error document.

- Amazon EC2 Deployment

Launch Instance: Launched a t3.micro instance with Ubuntu AMI. Ensure Port 80 (HTTP) is open in the security group.

Install Apache: Connect via SSH and run:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y apache2
sudo systemctl start apache2


Deploy Source: - Change permissions: sudo chown -R ubuntu:ubuntu /var/www/html

Use nano /var/www/html/index.html to create and paste the portfolio code.

Repeat for survey.html and error.html.

Error Page Config: - Edit /etc/apache2/apache2.conf to change AllowOverride None to AllowOverride All for /var/www/html.

Add ErrorDocument 404 /error.html at the bottom and restart Apache.

3. File Manifest

index.html: Homepage with bio and project links.

survey.html: Form for collecting prospective student feedback.

error.html: Custom 404 page.

readme.md: Deployment guide and URLs.